 is common in Japan to use ready-made roux, for making Japanese curry, which comes in a block from a box. The roux can also be cooked from scratch. The hard-paste roux melts from the heat and blends with the water to create a thick stew. Milk can also be used as a replacement for water to make the stew more creamy."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-cream-stew"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_stew"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Yoshoku","cuisine/yoshoku"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Roux","ingredient/roux"]]},{"h":"More from Yoshoku","links":[["Chicken katsu","dish/chicken-katsu"],["Doria (food)","dish/doria-food"],["Hayashi rice","dish/hayashi-rice"],["Menchi-katsu","dish/menchi-katsu"],["Naporitan","dish/naporitan"],["Tonkatsu","dish/tonkatsu"],["Toruko rice","dish/toruko-rice"],["Volga rice","dish/volga-rice"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/f/f1/Cone_Cream_Stew.jpg/500px-Cone_Cream_Stew.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Kuha455405","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cone_Cream_Stew.jpg"}},"dish/kangaroo-meat":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kangaroo-meat","n":"Kangaroo meat","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Australian cuisine","dot":"#55b8ad","intro":[["Kangaroo meat is produced in Australia from wild kangaroos and is exported to over 61 overseas markets."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kangaroo-meat"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangaroo_meat"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Australian cuisine","cuisine/australian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Belly Rumbles: Australian Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"