sekage, kransekake (Norwegian) or kransakaka (Icelandic) is a traditional Danish and Norwegian confection, often eaten on special occasions in Scandinavia. In English, the name means 'wreath cake'. In Norway it is alternatively referred to as tårnkake (English: 'tower cake') and often prepared for Constitution Day celebrations, Christmas, weddings, and baptisms. In Denmark it is typically eaten as part of New Year celebrations, while a variation of the cake, overflødighedshorn (English: 'cornucopia'), is traditionally served at weddings and baptisms."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kransekage"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kransekage"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Danish cuisine","cuisine/danish-cuisine"],["Norwegian cuisine","cuisine/norwegian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Egg white","ingredient/egg-white"],["Prunus dulcis","ingredient/prunus-dulcis"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]},{"h":"More from Danish cuisine","links":[["Æbleflæsk","dish/blefl-sk"],["Æbleskiver","dish/bleskiver"],["Danish pastry","dish/danish-pastry"],["Glögg","dish/glogg"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Labskaus","dish/labskaus"],["Risalamande","dish/risalamande"],["Rødgrød","dish/r-dgr-d"],["Smørrebrød","dish/sm-rrebr-d"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/6/6b/Kransekake.jpg/500px-Kransekake.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Kjetil Ree","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kransekake.jpg"}},"dish/krupnik-soup":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/krupnik-soup","n":"Krupnik (soup)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Krupnik is a thick Polish soup made from vegetable or meat broth, containing potatoes and barley groats (kasza jęczmienna, archaically called krupy—hence the name). Common additional ingredients include włoszczyzna (carrots, parsley, leek, and celery), onion, meat, and dried mushrooms."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-krupnik-soup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krupnik_(soup)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine"],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine"],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Barley","ingredient/barley"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Groat","ingredient/groat"],["Groats","ingredient/groats"],["Potatoes","ingredient/potatoes"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Polonist","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polonist.com","note":"Polish recipes and food culture from a Polish-born writer living abroad.","url":"https://www.polonist.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Polish Your Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polishyourkitchen.com","note":"Long-running blog of traditional Polish home recipes.","url":"https://polishyourkitchen.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Savas Kitchen: Ukrainian recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"savaskitchen.com","note":"Ukrainian-born home cook Nataliia Savas's section of family Ukrainian recipes.","url":"https://savaskitchen.com/category/ukrainian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Belarusian cuisine","links":[["Angel wings","dish/angel-wings"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Cold beet soup","dish/cold-beet-soup"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Kalduny","dish/kalduny"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Paska (bread)","dish/paska-bread"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Šakotis","dish/sakotis"],["Salceson","dish/salceson"],["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Syrniki","dish/syrniki"],["Zatiruha","dish/zatiruha"],["Zrazy","dish/zrazy"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/9/98/Krupnik_zupa.jpg/500px-Krupnik_zupa.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Mariuszjbie","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krupnik_zupa.jpg"}},"dish/mapo-tofu":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mapo-tofu","n":"Mapo tofu","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Mapo tofu is a popular Chinese dish from Sichuan province. It consists of tofu set in a spicy sauce, typically a thin, oily, and bright red suspension, based on douban (fermented broad bean and chili paste), and douchi (fermented black beans), along with minced meat, traditionally beef. Variations exist with other ingredients such as water chestnuts, onions, other vegetables, or wood ear fungus. It is likely to have originated at a Chengdu restaurant in the 1860s–1870s."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mapo-tofu"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mapo_tofu"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Doubanjiang","ingredient/doubanjiang"],["Douchi","ingredient/douchi"],["Tofu","ingredient/tofu"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Red House Spice","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gans